The details of the different classes appears in the Nethack Guidebook.
If you don't have one of those, you might be able to find it at the
ftp site, probably in a 'src' or 'doc' directory.

Each class has some advantages and disadvantages, and they are best
understood by actually trying to play those classes.  A comparison
here before you try it out may not be very informative.

It should be obvious that class that sound like Fighters will
Fight better than those that don't.  The non-fighter classes
have a bunch of useful differences, many of which are identifiable
from the equipment which each starts with.

To get the most of the first few games, I'd recommend playing in
Discovery mode (either include '-X' on the command line, or type
'X' as a command when the game is in progress.)  That will give
you more chances to get a feel for the game (you don't have to
worry about dying).

Finally, when you Do end a game, for whatever reason, take a good
look at your intrinsics as you leave.  They may also give you a clue
regarding differences between the classes, and maybe some other
special things that might have happened to you during the course
of the game.

Hope this is enough to get you started.  I'm deliberately trying to
avoid giving away too much of the interesting tidbits before you
get your feet wet.

